  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Galinsoga parviflora」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galinsoga_parviflora",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1376104256,
      "text": "Galinsoga parviflora is a species of herbaceous plant in the daisy family Asteraceae. It has several common names including guasca (Colombia), pacpa yuyo, paco yuyo, and waskha (Peru), burrionera (Ecuador), albahaca silvestre and saetilla (Argentina), mielcilla, piojito, galinsoga, gallant soldier, quickweed, and potato weed."
    }
  },
